msgid "Why Streamable HTTP Matters"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is taking the developer world by storm, and "
"now, with its latest spec update: Streamable HTTP support has arrived!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We're thrilled to announce that Quarkus MCP Server is the very first Java-"
"based MCP server SDK to embrace this innovation, making it easier than ever "
"for you to build, experiment, and deploy MCP-powered solutions—wherever you "
"need them."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkiverse/quarkus-mcp-server/releases/tag/1.2.0[Quarkus "
"MCP Server 1.2] now supports Streamable HTTP alongside `stdio` and `SSE` "
"transports. This enables new possibilities for connecting your MCP servers "
"to mobile apps and cloud services. While the implementation is fully "
"functional, some advanced features like https://modelcontextprotocol.io/"
"specification/2025-03-26/basic/transports#resumability-and-"
"redelivery[Resumability and Redelivery] are planned for future releases."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Streamable HTTP is the approach MCP spec have taken for real-time, "
"efficient, and scalable communication between clients and servers. It opens "
"the door to new integrations and user experiences, especially for platforms "
"and devices where traditional transports like SSE or stdio aren't ideal."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"And now, thanks to Quarkus MCP Server, Java developers are at the forefront "
"of this evolution. Whether you're building AI assistants, developer tools, "
"or next-gen chatbots, Streamable HTTP gives you the flexibility to reach "
"more users, faster."
msgstr ""

msgid "Easy upgrade"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Ready to try it out? Just update your Maven dependency to the latest Quarkus "
"MCP Server SSE transport:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"That's it! You're now equipped to serve Streamable HTTP from your Java MCP "
"server."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Want to see how to write your own MCP server? Check out our previous post: "
"https://quarkus.io/blog/mcp-server/[Introducing MCP Servers]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus MCP Servers: Power and Simplicity"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The https://github.com/quarkiverse/quarkus-mcp-servers[Quarkus MCP Servers "
"project] brings a suite of ready-to-use MCP servers, all built on Quarkus. "
"With version 1.0.0.CR4, streamable HTTP support is baked in—no extra "
"configuration required. We just updated the dependency, and it was ready to "
"go!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To enable Streamable HTTP, simply launch any server in Quarkus MCP Servers "
"with the `--sse` flag:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Connecting Clients"
msgstr ""

msgid "The default URL for Streamable HTTP is:"
msgstr ""

msgid "(For SSE, use `http://<your-ip>:8080/mcp/sse` as before.)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"While Streamable HTTP is still new, some pioneering clients already support "
"it. Notably, the open source iOS app https://github.com/daodao97/"
"chatmcp\"[ChatMCP] (available on https://testflight.apple.com/join/"
"dCXksFJV[TestFlight]) and a non-open source version on the https://apps."
"apple.com/dk/app/chatmcp/id6745196560[iOS App Store] both work seamlessly "
"with MCP and support or even require Streamable HTTP."
msgstr ""

msgid "Here's a quick demo of ChatMCP in action with the jvminsight server:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Kotlin: Lightweight and Fun"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus supports both Java and Kotlin, giving you flexibility in how you "
"build your MCP servers. Want to experiment? Here's a playful example of a "
"Kotlin MCP server you can run instantly with JBang. It fetches a random "
"image from https://picsum.photos/ and returns it as a base64-encoded image, "
"as the MCP spec requires."
msgstr ""

msgid "Save this as `demo.kt` and run it with:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can now use the `randomimage` tool in ChatMCP or any other MCP client "
"that supports Streamable HTTP. It's that easy—and a great way to start "
"experimenting!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Streamable HTTP is an important step for the MCP ecosystem, and Quarkus MCP "
"Server is putting Java developers in the driver's seat. Whether you're "
"building tools, bots, or entirely new experiences, now's the perfect time to "
"dive in and see what you can create."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We can't wait to see what you build. Try it out, share your feedback, and "
"help shape the future of MCP — powered by Quarkus!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Have fun!"
msgstr ""
